      "category": "integration",
      "cause": "`concurrency-scope` was added to `reusable-test-rust-build.yml` but not to the wrapper `reusable-rust-build.yml` that most callers use, and the group key drops `inputs.job-name`, so nothing distinguishes two wrapper invocations in one caller workflow.",
      "checklist_ids": [
        1
      ],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "description": "The new job concurrency group for `reusable-test-rust-build` is keyed on callee + caller repository + caller workflow + ref + `concurrency-scope`, and omits `inputs.job-name` (unlike `reusable-rust-test.yml:440`, which includes it). docs/workflow-contract.md:600-602 tells callers that a workflow invoking the same reusable twice on one ref must pass a distinct `concurrency-scope`. But the in-repo public wrapper `.github/workflows/reusable-rust-build.yml` exposes no `concurrency-scope` input and forwards only `job-name` (lines 190-200), so a caller workflow with two `reusable-rust-build` jobs (e.g. two build scripts / two crates) puts both nested jobs in the identical group with `cancel-in-progress: true`, and the second silently cancels the first with no available mitigation. P3 because the single-call path this PR targets is correct and the pre-existing ref-only key collided too; what remains is the missing plumbing for the documented remedy.",
      "evidence_style": "cross_file",
      "file": ".github/workflows/reusable-test-rust-build.yml",
      "fingerprint": "42f629dabacc35ca",
      "fix": "Either add a `concurrency-scope` input to `reusable-rust-build.yml` and forward it in the `uses:` block, or include `inputs.job-name` in the group key (as `reusable-rust-test.yml` already does) so distinct required-check names deconflict automatically.",
      "line": 215,
      "ordinal": 1,
      "severity": "P3",
      "since_round": 1,
      "status": "open",
      "title": "concurrency-scope escape hatch unreachable via rust-build wrapper"
    },
