      "confidence": "high",
      "description": "The new regression guard greps for `description:` and `${{` on the *same physical line*. Most action.yml files in this repo write descriptions as folded block scalars (`description: >-` with the text on following lines \u2014 e.g. `.github/actions/validate-runner-policy/action.yml:5`, `create-signed-commit/action.yml:24`, `prepare-pypi-upload/action.yml:29`), so reintroducing `${{ runner.os }}` on a continuation line of a folded description would not match and the guard would pass while GitHub still fails the action with \"Unrecognized named-value\". The same hole applies to the other non-templated metadata fields (`name:`, `author:`, `branding:`), which fail identically. P3 because the fix itself is correct and the guard does catch the exact single-line form that caused #1076; only regression coverage is incomplete.",
